{
  "summary": "This experiment tested a multiprofile RNA-only model using the scvi_n200 encoder with avgpool aggregation, achieving validation accuracy of 0.6501 (F1: 0.6275), surpassing the previous pca_n2000-based multiprofile baseline (0.5907 accuracy). The result suggests the RNA encoder type may influence performance in multiprofile settings, but uncertainty remains about whether other factors, such as data distribution or model architecture, could also contribute to the observed improvement."
}

